From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:43:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: skip the EFI reset path when restarting from a panic
 in interrupt context

ResetSystem() runs EFI runtime services, which fault when invoked from
interrupt context (softlockup/hardlockup panic). On the Surface Pro 11
the EFI reset from IRQ context oopses and wedges instead of rebooting.
Fall through to the PSCI restart handler in that case. Restarts from
process context, including other panics, still go through ResetSystem().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/process.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
index 581f80e9b9b7..90651cb8144d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
@@ -135,9 +135,14 @@ void machine_restart(char *cmd)
 
 	/*
 	 * UpdateCapsule() depends on the system being reset via
-	 * ResetSystem().
+	 * ResetSystem().  However ResetSystem() runs EFI runtime services,
+	 * which fault if invoked from interrupt context (e.g. a softlockup
+	 * or hardlockup panic).  There, skip the EFI reset and leave it to
+	 * the PSCI restart handler, which resets cleanly from any context.
+	 * (SP11/X1E80100: EFI reset from IRQ context oopses and wedges
+	 * instead of rebooting.)
 	 */
-	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES))
+	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES) && !in_interrupt())
 		efi_reboot(reboot_mode, NULL);
 
 	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
